  "measures": [],
  "notes": "Read in a real browser. All 66 sample ballots are scanned image PDFs (no text layer); each was rendered and read visually. Supervisors elected at large, vote for three. The county is split into East and West Pottawattamie Soil & Water Conservation Districts and East and West Pottawattamie Agricultural Extension districts - voters get one of each based on location (East: Avoca/Carson/Hancock/Macedonia/Oakland/Walnut areas; West: Council Bluffs, Carter Lake, Crescent, Minden, Neola, Treynor, Underwood, Boomer/Neola Twp, etc.). East Ag Extension has 4 candidates for 5 seats. Township offices with no printed candidate (write-in only) are listed with empty candidate arrays (e.g., Garner, Layton, Rockford trustee and clerk; Garner and James trustee vacancies). Lewis Township trustee is vote-for-two. Council Bluffs (Kane Twp), Carter Lake, Waveland Township and city-only ballots show no township offices. No county hospital trustee race. Page 2 of every ballot checked: no county, city or school public measures (only Statewide Public Measure 1)."
}